course: dictionary
lesson: 6769
title: One word, two animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An opossum is an animal from North and South America. Like a kangaroo, it is a marsupial: its tiny babies grow in a pouch on the mother's body. «The opossum is a marsupial, like a kangaroo: its babies grow in a pouch and then ride on their mother's back.»
explain: The same word can mean different animals in different places. In America, an opossum has a pointed white face, bare ears and a long, bare tail. In Australia and New Zealand, «possum» is a different, furry tree animal. Check where the text is set, and read the sentence, to know which one is meant.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «When badly frightened, an opossum may play dead: it falls over, stays still and gives off a bad smell; this is called playing possum.» The words after the colon explain what play dead means, so you do not need a dictionary to understand it.
fact: An opossum is a North and South American marsupial about the size of a cat.
fact: A marsupial is an animal whose babies grow in a pouch.
fact: «Playing possum» means pretending to be dead: the animal falls over, stays still and smells bad.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «possum» is a different, furry tree animal.
fact: In New Zealand, introduced Australian possums are pests that damage forests and birds.
exercise: «The opossum is a marsupial, like a kangaroo: its babies grow in a pouch.» What is a marsupial? | A tree that grows in forests | *An animal whose babies grow in a pouch | An animal with a hard shell | A bird that cannot fly
exercise: «A raccoon, an opossum and a skunk each have four legs, one tail and a coat of fur.» How many tails does an opossum have? | Three | None | *One | Two
exercise: Kai reads that an animal will «play possum». What does the phrase mean? | To sing a loud song | *To pretend to be dead by falling still | To hide food for the winter | To climb a tall tree to escape
test: Which place uses «possum» for a furry tree animal? | Brazil | Mexico | *Australia | Canada
test: «The Virginia opossum may fall over, go stiff, drool and smell bad when terrified.» What does terrified mean? | Slightly tired | Hungry for food | *Extremely frightened | Very happy
exam: Why might an opossum play dead? | *To make predators lose interest, because it seems dead | To get attention from people | To hide its babies from its mother | To swim across a river
